  "description": "#5140 Phase 5 — `apply_page_source` with `merge`: a save whose base is stale folds the changes the page took since into the buffer instead of being refused. Blocks pair by id across the base, the page's source now and the buffer, whose text carries its ids beside its lines (`lineIds`, #5160 A); a block one side edited takes that edit, a block edited both ways is kept twice (the buffer's version as a new block before the page's), a block deleted on the page and edited or moved to another parent in the buffer comes back as a new block, a block dropped from the buffer and edited or moved to another parent on the page stays, and the side that moved a block places it. Only what the tauri mock models: plain single-line text, no properties or names, as in `apply_page_source.json`. Payload ops change the page between the merged saves; each `merge` step's `baseSource` is the source an earlier step left, so it is stale, except the fresh-base step. One kind of write per step, and the steps that create a block come after every step whose base they would otherwise have to spell. Seed: S1 (Home) > S2 (alpha), S3 (bravo), S4 (charlie), S5 (delta), S6 (echo). Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
